I first started playing Nethack at Varsity in 1997, so I'm guessing
version 3.2 or so. I was completely unspoilt, and made it to the castle
a few times, completed the quest a few times, but never got any
further. My class mates were more interested in another game Crossfire,
a realtime multiplayer game with a lot of similarities.  I hadn't
played computer games for many years, when one of my old varsity
friends mentioned he'd downloaded crossfire, and was interested in a
session.

This got me thinking about Nethack, and I donwloaded the Win32 binary,
and fired it up.  I found lots of neat changes from memory, not least
being the tiles interface, and played a few games.  However I kept
getting really frustrated, and resorting to save scumming.  I probably
didn't even need to, with a bit of thought I could have got out of the
problem, but it became a crutch.  I needed a way to overcome this, and
learn to play properly. I lurked on here a few weeks, picked up lots of
hints, and eventually threw away all my local characters, and logged
into NAO.

Hello Olias, the gnomish Healer

