Dlvl:1  $:0 HP:12(12) Pw:6(6) AC:8  Xp:1/1 T:1

My first challenge was playing without tiles again, having got used to
them.  This caused me to play quite slowly and cautiosly to start with
- not to mention make a few mistakes!

The RNG was in a funny humour throughout the entire game. My first
evidence of this was a lack of tools. I generally rely on my pets a
lot, so a whistle is the first order of business for me. Throughout the
entire game, I did not find a single magic whistle.  I've never
abandoned a pet before, but this game I must have left >20 scattered
around the dungeons.

Level two had a bookshop, with three scrolls of identify, none of which
stacked - so one was blessed.  My first guess ID'd everything - the RNG
liked me. I robbed the store blind, and a jewelry store on lvl 3, and
headed into the mines on lvl 4, with 2000 gold.

My large dog kept me alive through the mines, which were mostly dark.
Minetown was the Grotto, and the priest was cross-aligned.  I bought
some protection, BUC checked all my armour, and checked all the shops -
no light sources other than candles.

A tattered cape I'd found earlier turned out to be a cloak of
displacement, so (still at level 1, and with AC-3, and displacement) I
headed back up and down to Sokoban.  Stone to fleshed meatballs allowed
me to tame heaps of dogs and cats on the way, but without a leash or
whistle, many were left behind. In Sokoban, I failed to kill a werewolf
quickly enough (and forgot cloaks of displacement only give MC2) and
got lycanthropy. Hermes was nice enough to heal me - next turn:
The werejackal bites --more--
You feel feverish.

After waiting a few thousand turns so I could pray again (and summoning
lots of nice jackal friends to guard me all the while), I turned back
into a human, and earned myself a nice new BoH, so my St: 10 Healer
could actually move around without burdening himself.

With no reflection, and no MR, I was loathe to go too deep, but slowly
worked my way down.  Around DL 12 I found an AoR, and decided to risk
Mines End without MR. Stepped on 1 polymorph trap - became a nymph -
then found a ring of polycontrol, and next time I stepped on a
polymorph trap I became a new gnome.

Around turn 35000, with AC:-9 and HP:181 I began the quest, using a
wand of cold to get over the water.  5 gray and silver dragons, and no
scales.  Eventually I think a red dragon dropped some scales, which I
wore for a few hundred turns, until on the level above the cyclops a
silver dragon finally did.  I swapped, and enchanted them to armour.
and then went to wake the cyclops.  Olias lost 5 levels, but his trusty
wand of anaesthetic, and expert +5 unicorn horn saved the day.  With
new staff in hand, he headed down past medusa (Titan), back up to check
Perseus (had levitation boots - yay!), then headed for the castle.  The
castle was fairly easy, and the WoW was 0:1. Wishes:
 - 2 blessed scrolls of charging - got 1
 - recharge
 - CoMR - finally, breathed much easier once had this on!!
 - Speed boots
 - Magic marker
 - wrested last wish for a
 - Helm of Brilliance - casting Magic Mapping at less than 100% fail.
I still hadn't found any scrolls of Geno, and had no wishes left, so
decided to try and play geno-less.  This made hell a wee bit more
interesting, with Lichs playing havoc. About 100 turns into hell, (And
200 turns after wishing for the CoMR!) I got Touch of Deathed. The
mysterious force was a pain, took me about 12 tries to get up 5 levels
to lvl 45, then it left me alone the entire rest of the way.

Got back to level 1, stock take: No gold detection!  Whip out magic
marker, write it. You have no knowledge of that spell!! I had finally
found a magic lamp in hell, so burn it, wish for 2 ?oGD.  They are
DAIYEN FOOELS.  Now came my biggest mistake of the game - I thought I
could just specify that descriptor to write - but it didn't let me.
More wasted charges. Got 25 left - oh well, if I can't write GD, I'll
write a ?oCharging for my wand of death. Leaves 5 chrges.  Then a brain
wave - I should have ID'd the ?ofGD!!!  cast ID, try to write again -
marker runs dry.  So, I have two scrolls of GD.  Earth I manage
without, Air I try without, but use one.  I REALLY want to save the
last for water, so wander around on fire forever, until a salamander
finally dissapears.

On Astral, I arrive on the right, with Death.  Start heading that way,
Arch and Master Liches start appearing everywhere.  I kill death, but
can't get through the hordes, so back pedal, and head for Famine in the
middle altar.  Get in there no problem, it's Hermes'!! Woot.

So, my first game on NAO, and I ascend.  Cool.  Have to try again now
:-)

Olias, neutral male gnomish Healer



